.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T21:55:13-07:00","id":1316194,"title":"","content":"Great sheet! It's 100x more complete than the standard<br /> <br /> I don't know if you're still iterating, but if you are, I had a couple of notes to make it just slightly more complete:<ul><li>Callings should have space for keywords (maybe move the name and dots to the left?)</li> <li>Knacks could use a checkbox for whether they're slotted, as well as a way of denoting Heroic vs Immortal knacks</li> <li>A space (potentially a full page with room for description) for completed Deeds. It would be useful if the first one was hardcoded as &quot;Visitation&quot;</li> <li>Relics are associated with completed Deeds. Maybe a small box to put the Deed # (from the above-mentioned page)?</li> <li>the Purview boxes could use more space for innate powers. If possible, take away from the Purview name box (even Yaoyorozu-No-Kamigami only just over half-fills)</li> </ul>And a few minor details<ul><li>&quot;defence&quot; --&gt; &quot;defense&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Bonds&quot; font on page 5 is a bit odd</li> <li>Guides have dots pre-filled</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]}